      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting an \"Access Denied\" error when my lambda function tries to write logs to this s3 bucket. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u look at this policy and tell me what i missed?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your policy correctly grants permission to put objects into the bucket, which is necessary for logging. However, you might also need to ensure the IAM Role attached to your Lambda function has the necessary permissions to *invoke* the S3 API, although `s3:PutObject` is the main action. Double-check that the execution role for your Lambda function is explicitly attached and correctly configured in the AWS console. Sometimes, regional misconfigurations or lack of `s3:ListBucket` access (if you were reading) can also cause issues.",
